{
 "id": "2022-fu-rural",
 "name": "Rural Community Streets: Restorative Potential of Nine Street Types",
 "description": "Faithful replication of the silent-photo condition (S0) with the paper's own photographs: participants view nine street photographs from four rural communities in Pidu District, Chengdu, one for each street type (artificial / natural / artificial-natural enclosure; artificial / natural semi-enclosed; artificial-natural and natural-artificial semi-enclosure; artificial / natural open), each full screen for 30 s, imagining being in the scene. After each photo they rate the paper's six statements on a 0-4 agreement scale: four restorative components scale items (being away, extent, fascination, compatibility), tranquility and visual aesthetic quality. Rebuilt from Fu, Ren, Li & Zhang (2022), Frontiers in Public Health 10: 861072, with the nine photographs and the questionnaire wording from its Supplementary Material (CC BY 4.0). Analysis as in the paper: Cronbach's alpha; mean RCS score per street type with ANOVA across the nine types; Pearson correlations between VAQ and the RCS items. Differences from the original study: (1) only the silent-image condition S0 is included; the paper also played each photo with three birdsong/traffic-noise mixes at 55 dB(A), whose audio files are not published; (2) no pulse or blood-pressure measurement; (3) online rather than one by one in a soundproof lab; (4) the paper does not report the presentation order; here the photos appear in random order; (5) photos are resized to 1600 x 1200 px; (6) the residence question and its options are our wording.",
 "author": "Fu, Ren, Li & Zhang",
